[{"id":"VRCE-3-52-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":1,"english":"Carried away (by Ravana), Vaidehi, not finding any defender, five principal monkeys stationed on the top of a hill.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.903,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f5f3a94e6ddaea491477115a105b6221e1d43036ae41530839f56f9086ba588e","compact":"138ba6d858a33ec58d4ddb2789c1e90725456eed4c8d0ed5926b28ab4c9f554f","nasal":"9f61c44fd48e19e7fb163e41cb3535c74a29a24027667bedc2240b562d45120d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":2,"english":"Thereat, that lady of expansive eyes and surpassing charms, in the hope that they might convey the intelligence to Rāma, flung off in their midst her gold-gleaming silken sheet, and elegant ornaments.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.931,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eed87df3a7221fb9b83728f52fbab2b56bf446dc3dab714b40d85efbf2802dd9","compact":"e16c3673a20e4e9795d5102c84d3dae42bcc1cb4ee5d1624265a77e95b3b2d32","nasal":"e16c3673a20e4e9795d5102c84d3dae42bcc1cb4ee5d1624265a77e95b3b2d32"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":3,"english":"But the Ten headed one owing to hurry did not observe the throwing of the cloth along with the ornaments. Those foremost of monkeys having tawny eyes observes with winkless eyes the large-eyed Sītā as she was giving way to grief.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.243,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891