ignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2a6857fcc19af52c1b22c042d771638861333c47f41ab40bb0e53cd13f04e37f","compact":"4d34f7f33b36e8658ca53ffcfd8d567981542f8c39ab28eadd363ee4a452a748","nasal":"5c3593da2d882203a4a25e373184577a8c7556f3c2bdd69d5ca181f67faa7cc5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":7,"english":"And speedily, like an arrow shot from a bow, he, coursing the welkin, left behind woods and streams and mountains and pieces of water.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16db5beae6a48814d2e1ed6e3c35fffff95b99342d5a113181b527a1dc11227f","compact":"96152276dfb02840af4af06873bc054964d414cbb66658d8075c4297ea6b8402","nasal":"96152276dfb02840af4af06873bc054964d414cbb66658d8075c4297ea6b8402"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":8,"english":"Coming to the abode of Varuņa, that refuge of rivers, the exhaustless ocean—the home of whales and alligators, he crossed over it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b927360fef2fe75bfb0aeb8acf6ed1cd1edd8dd9e2dac4ee5783791f8d79edb","compact":"703c05f1ebee9bb0810da5a27851890ccab6dd07e55987e71ec7a0a200c2d779","nasal":"703c05f1ebee9bb0810da5a27851890ccab6dd07e55987e71ec7a0a200c2d779"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":9,"english":"In consequence of the carrying away of Vaidehi, Varuna's abode, from grief, had all its waves stilled and its fishes and mighty snakes inert.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12f50c5817c8674bf5694649547f45bc2b2fb6715bdb28f965d003241527c084","compact":"fbecd1ca14bec8aa51c01a67e48a2cb175b238e340b30621699dea9207165544","nasal":"fbecd1ca14bec8aa51c01a67e48a2cb175b238e340b30621699dea9207165544"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":10,"english":"And the Cāranas uttered in the heavens these words, O Ten-headed one, this is your end. Thus did the Siddhas then say.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8507820742b5e809fb04fca2547e20bc35565ab2bb9eeab60cde1af7faf61b5b","compact":"6898744ffb96160f2c267c083cb2f2f770caeef5e6cdc3a0d6f3a0807224173b","nasal":"d794012bfeb5a445ffad68a434e79b498b5b59f906febad967677072791c2833"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":11,"english":"And taking Sītā on his lap, representing his own Death, who endeavoured (to liberate herself). Rāvana entered the city of Lankā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07a23e440923db0d7a1bf2b5533a9be596823f7b194b8aaf5e6dfc2ca1781a84","compact":"ea18b1d4c6035940b9737ef2112c9d998ae476c53f99c43bcb9f4e9883f8fdd2","nasal":"b5cdc9cd23d7e30df9fbb5bda3a2cdd7775881196d227646a745255a76ecec82"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":12,"english":"And entering the city of Lankā, vast, with all its highways well-arranged, and with people thronging its gates, he entered his own inner apartment.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"448fd5fd1bb727ec398034361f913453efafb5618be83331fb584100d5f1e4e6","compact":"741c87c5455d84c960ae4e43fb44e087b3931f6c757255bfa4d7159126dbf28d","nasal":"6e37cf45004de9725b42a12d2b36bad01742fd62dd4218a7ea909d420a995511"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":13,"english":"Then Rāvana set Sītā there, having eyes with dark outer corners, exercised with grief and dole; as if Máyā had set his own Asura Illusion (in his own palace).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"190a7fa57f58586eb08f6f5d160135fcd52f78e2dc718411372dc2731e873ad3","compact":"912b257c531885520bedf350d8d42f1e49f00cda058f3d91199b0deb5ee616d4","nasal":"bc376190a1d04aa59d788151e52abb3cc62699a85278cfc7fa3c06963b01fee7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":14,"english":"Then the Ten-headed one spoke to some female friends of terrible visages, Let no man or woman behold Sītā without my permission.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.791,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"996c745e3c5b4b510f17b1a7f8f5a081e2f7a9e498d310e23c0f29e68c19da0c","compact":"3a4b34bca097a9