 Janasthāna-that field of carnage-which ere this contained the abode of Khara; and casting off fear at a distance, do you sojourn in vacant Janasthāna with all its Raksasas slain (by Rama).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.908,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"721b31fc6685fdddba9b83db39233b7f8acb04e5f84576f8ec631c4f0a23277c","compact":"d0c09839a37063e5e35be39346be3915ae4bdb22105d8dd81b7fd1075184b044","nasal":"d0c09839a37063e5e35be39346be3915ae4bdb22105d8dd81b7fd1075184b044"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":21,"english":"A great many troops endued with exceeding prowess, who had been posted in Janasthāna, have, along with Düşana and Khara, been slain by the shafts of Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.473,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f1f7b43685dc5c6234a959ab38a5263a76ecd7ab60bc4104cfd79cae4efa3e3","compact":"3ae69a43b8f56f38dc56fb5e2dd069d93abff221b609d5b1aedb677e5489ef89","nasal":"3ae69a43b8f56f38dc56fb5e2dd069d93abff221b609d5b1aedb677e5489ef89"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-52-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":52,"verse":22,"english":"Hence unprecedented is my wrath, towering above my patience; and great and fierce also is the hostility I have conceived against Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-54-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3052022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12fa66723aef0aba4eda56068b8b24abecc33d8c015d23bb051434d350df4f10","compact":"e24fb99200d43e3b44d9a83d9e174d2